The Wolffish Cloud go-to-market lives at `~/gtm/Wolffish-GTM-Brain` and is the source of truth for
positioning, messaging, claims and voice. Change that path if the brain is checked out elsewhere.

Read in this order before writing anything customer-facing: `AGENTS.md`, then
`rules/writing-rules.md`, `rules/do-not-say.md`, `rules/feature-status.md` and `rules/glossary.md`.
For any channel task load `reference/relationship-engine.md`, which is the channel engine.

Pick the audience first and never blend them: the security officer, the finance director, and the
partner-reached institutions of ICP 2.

Non-negotiables. Kingdom of Saudi Arabia only. No proof point outside the closed set in
`ops/copy-bank.md`, because there is no reference customer yet. Every capability carries its status
flag in the same sentence. Landed cost on both sides, never the seat price alone against a
competitor seat price. Never position against HUMAIN, neutralise in one sentence. Nothing flagged
IN BUILD or ROADMAP is demonstrated. Automated outreach sequencing, volume cold email and paid
social are refused: decline, say why in one sentence, offer the in-scope alternative.

Run `ops/QA-checklist.md` against the draft before returning it. New market input goes to
`ops/signal-log.md` first, never straight into the copy.
